1 NOTE Great-grandfather of Miles (father of Joan Liebes Hutson). Son of Julien and
2 CONT Sophie Liebes and grandson of Herman Liebes, founder of H. Liebes & Co. At 13
2 CONT he nearly drowned at Long Beach, California (July 1916) riding on his
2 CONT father's back in the surf; a lifeguard pulled him out, but his father died.
2 CONT Married Edith Wormser in San Francisco, January 1923. Followed the family
2 CONT fur trade: Portland (where Joan was born, 1931), San Francisco (1939-40), then
2 CONT Dallas (c. 1942), where he became Neiman-Marcus's fur buyer and a vice
2 CONT president. In May 1966 he paid a record $1,100 per skin for 40 "Black
2 CONT Willow" mink at the Hudson's Bay Company auction for an $80,000 coat, and in
2 CONT 1968 AP reported he paid the highest price for sea-otter pelts since 1911. He
2 CONT headed the Fur Information and Fashion Council's program in 1959.
2 CONT IDENTIFICATION: the San Francisco News Letter wedding notice names him "Mr.
2 CONT George Julien Liebes, son of Mrs. Julien Liebes," marrying Edith Wormser -
2 CONT matching "George J. Liebes" and wife "Edith M." in the 1950 census and
2 CONT "George and Edith Liebes" in Joan's obituary. The census age (49) implies
2 CONT b. ~1901, while the 1916 news report implies ~1903. Death not yet documented.
2 SOUR @S15@
3 _CONF Secondary
2 SOUR @S12@
3 _CONF Primary
2 SOUR @S14@
3 _CONF Secondary
2 SOUR @S16@
3 _CONF Secondary
