1 OCCU Furrier; founder of H. Liebes & Co., San Francisco (1864); organizer of the North American Commercial Company (Alaska fur-seal lease)
2 SOUR @S20@
3 _CONF Secondary
1 NOTE Great-great-great-grandfather of Miles - the Ashkenazi immigrant ancestor of
2 CONT the Liebes line. Born in Rawicz, Prussia (a Jewish community in the Posen
2 CONT province, now Poland), he worked briefly for a New York furrier, then with
2 CONT partner Charles J. Behlow opened a small fur manufactory in San Francisco in
2 CONT October 1864. H. Liebes & Co. became the leading fur house on the Pacific
2 CONT Coast, with stores in San Francisco and Portland ("indisputably the largest
2 CONT dealers in sealskins in the world"). He helped organize the North American
2 CONT Commercial Company, which held the U.S. Alaska fur-seal lease, owned vessels
2 CONT trading to Alaska, and was active in B'nai B'rith and Congregation Emanu-El.
2 CONT The business was incorporated in 1890 with a capital of $1,000,000.
2 SOUR @S20@
3 _CONF Secondary
2 SOUR @S10@
