1 OCCU Actor; tutor; minister at Stony Creek (1743) and the Circular (Independent Congregational) Church, Charleston (1757)
2 SOUR @S29@
3 _CONF Secondary
1 NOTE 6x-great-grandfather of Miles and founder of the Hutson family of South
2 CONT Carolina. Began studying law at the Inns of Court but gave it up and came to
2 CONT America as an actor in 1740. Converted by George Whitefield's preaching in
2 CONT New York, he tutored for Hugh Bryan in Charles Town and worked at
2 CONT Whitefield's Bethesda Orphan House in Savannah. A church was built for him at
2 CONT Stony Creek in the Indian Land (Beaufort County) in 1743, and he was called to
2 CONT Charleston's Circular Church in 1757. Married (1) 1743 Mrs. Mary (Woodward)
2 CONT Chardon, who died 1757; (2) 10 Oct 1758 Mrs. Mary (Prioleau) Bryan. The
2 CONT family arms: "Per chevron embattled or and vert, three martlets
2 CONT countercharged." The surname Hutson is an English patronymic from the
2 CONT medieval given name Hudde (a pet form of Hugh).
