2 CONT 1619 aboard the Bona Nova as one of the settlers for the College Land at
2 CONT Henrico; listed as Lieutenant Thomas Osborne in the 1624-25 muster;
2 CONT represented the College in the House of Burgesses (1625); commissioned
2 CONT Captain by Gov. George Yeardley in 1627 to lead settlers against the
2 CONT Powhatan; settled "Coxendale" on the James River. The link to Margaret
2 CONT Osborne Lockett (as her grandfather) is the compiler's best reconstruction,
2 CONT not a documented fact.
