2 CONT plantations in Beaufort District, S.C.; attended South Carolina College;
2 CONT served in the Confederate Army throughout the Civil War in Virginia, North
2 CONT Carolina, and South Carolina; was a teacher and professor in several
2 CONT southern states, including fifteen years in Texas; and settled finally in
2 CONT New Orleans, La., as an artist and writer." Notes his father William F.
2 CONT Hutson signed the South Carolina Ordinance of Secession. See also 64
2 CONT Parishes (64parishes.org/entry/charles-woodward-hutson).
